      "message": "Should we implement this, eventually?\n\nDoes that even fix the problem?\n\nIf I understand the idea statement:\n 1. 2 interrupts fire (X and UART)\n 2. X is handled\n    a. cflush called, UART_IER(UARTN) \u0026\u003d ~UART_IER_THRI;\n 3. RV33 receives global VIC, UART_IER_THRI is not set so the handler crashes.\n\nI think I see how batch handling would solve that.\n\nBut now, this could still happen, right?\n\n 1. IRQ X fires\n 2. X is handled, and while handling:\n    a. UART IRQ fires.\n    b. cflush called, UART_IER(UARTN) \u0026\u003d ~UART_IER_THRI;\n 3. RV33 receives global VIC, UART_IER_THRI is not set so the handler crashes.",
